<BaseLayout title="Contact & Corrections" description="Report an outdated command, incorrect source, broken link, or site problem to the AI Agent Hub maintainer through the public website repository on GitHub." lang="en">
  <article class="card">
    <h1>Contact &amp; corrections</h1>
    <p>For a content correction, broken link, or website problem, use the site's existing GitHub issue tracker. Opening an issue requires a GitHub account.</p>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/duoglas/openclaw-hub/issues/new" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Open a website issue on GitHub →</a></p>
    <p>You can also <a href="https://github.com/duoglas/openclaw-hub/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">read existing reports</a> before filing a new one.</p>
    <h2>What to include</h2>
    <ul><li>The URL of the affected page and the section or sentence.</li><li>What you believe is wrong, with an official source or a minimal reproduction if possible.</li><li>For a technical guide: relevant product versions and sanitized error text.</li></ul>
    <h2>Keep private information out</h2>
    <p>Issues are public. Do not post tokens, passwords, personal addresses, billing records, or unredacted logs. This is a public feedback channel, not a private support or sensitive-data submission form.</p>
    <p>The maintainer may need more evidence before making a correction. No response-time commitment is made.</p>
    <p><a href="/en/about/">About the site</a> · <a href="/en/privacy/">Privacy &amp; ads</a></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
